00:02:35.291 --> 00:02:38.332
For two days, I had to
wrap my son in a towel.

00:02:38.332 --> 00:02:41.337
But something happened,
Steve, in those two days.

00:02:41.337 --> 00:02:42.840
I was at rock bottom.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.954
I was broke, and I was broken.

00:02:45.954 --> 00:02:48.600
Inglewood, California,
my son laying on his back

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.463
at eight months, I have a towel over him,

00:02:50.463 --> 00:02:52.640
and I have my hand on his stomach, saying,

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:55.384
"Don't you worry, J Lonny,

00:02:55.384 --> 00:02:58.187
"Mommy will never be this broke again."

00:02:58.187 --> 00:03:01.326
And I had made a decision I was bankrupt.

00:03:01.326 --> 00:03:04.151
And every stinking thinking I had,

00:03:04.151 --> 00:03:06.768
I was bankrupt and trying
to protect my pride.

00:03:06.768 --> 00:03:08.587
I was bankrupt and trying to be all that

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:11.705
and a bag of chips and a
bowl of grits falsified.

00:03:11.705 --> 00:03:14.573
I was bankrupt and trying
to not ask anyone for help.

00:03:14.573 --> 00:03:17.426
I was bankrupt in everything
that was holding me

00:03:17.426 --> 00:03:18.928
and keeping me where I was.

00:03:18.928 --> 00:03:20.696
I've always talked a good game,

00:03:20.696 --> 00:03:23.038
but I wasn't doing anything with my gift.

00:03:23.038 --> 00:03:24.750
And all that thing about potential,

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.844
I was tired of having potential,
I wanted to have my now.

00:03:27.844 --> 00:03:29.795
And I looked at that baby at eight months,

00:03:29.795 --> 00:03:33.167
