00:06:03.807 --> 00:06:05.772
None of that means my future.

00:06:05.772 --> 00:06:08.149
That's just the circumstance
that I came from.

00:06:08.149 --> 00:06:11.280
That's not what defines my
future, I just believe that.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.182
Not a lot validated it,

00:06:13.182 --> 00:06:15.843
but faith is believing
in the unseen anyway.

00:06:15.843 --> 00:06:17.858
So I had enough faith to go,

00:06:17.858 --> 00:06:21.335
"I know like I know like
I know like I know."

00:06:21.335 --> 00:06:23.494
I don't necessarily have to see it yet.

00:06:23.494 --> 00:06:25.142
Christy talked about affirmations.

00:06:25.142 --> 00:06:28.403
Abundant thinkers understand
the power of I am.

00:06:28.403 --> 00:06:30.366
Anything after the word I am

00:06:30.366 --> 00:06:33.523
is true to your unconscious
mine, Michael, anything.

00:06:33.523 --> 00:06:37.820
Anything after I am,
anything, anything after I am,

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.522
even if you're just
you know it's not true,

00:06:39.522 --> 00:06:41.124
your conscious mind will believe it.

00:06:41.124 --> 00:06:42.465
Anything after I am.

00:06:42.465 --> 00:06:45.056
So the use of affirmations
is very intentional

00:06:45.056 --> 00:06:46.723
and very consistent.

00:06:48.582 --> 00:06:52.582
I was diagnosed as
clinically depressed in 2001,

00:06:58.779 --> 00:07:00.329
1998, I'm sorry.

00:07:00.329 --> 00:07:02.856
I was diagnosed as clinically depressed.

00:07:02.856 --> 00:07:04.613
Me, it didn't make sense.

00:07:04.613 --> 00:07:06.241
I had been in a relationship,

00:07:06.241 --> 00:07:09.665
I was engaged to get married and my fiance

00:07:09.665 --> 00:07:13.273
who I didn't not know at
the time was bi-polar,

00:07:13.273 --> 00:07:14.901
and he'd stopped taking his medicines

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:19.309
and under the belief system
that love can cure anything.

00:07:19.309 --> 00:07:21.362
And so I ended up being picked up

00:07:21.362 --> 00:07:22.990
and thrown three feet across the room,

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:25.672
and I ended up being
choked until I passed out.

00:07:25.672 --> 00:07:27.274
And once I got out of that relationship,

00:07:27.274 --> 00:07:30.744
I just was different, was different.

00:07:30.744 --> 00:07:34.995
So my mom insisted that
I go to the doctor.

00:07:34.995 --> 00:07:38.278
I went to the doctor
and I sat on the table,

00:07:38.278 --> 00:07:40.592
and she checked me and talked to me

00:07:40.592 --> 00:07:43.653
and came back in with a
prescription and she said,

00:07:43.653 --> 00:07:46.944
"Lisa, you're clinically depressed."

00:07:46.944 --> 00:07:49.931
And I felt like I heard Charlie
Brown's parents talking,

00:07:49.931 --> 00:07:52.112
like whaa whaa, whaa whaa, whaa.

00:07:52.112 --> 00:07:53.687
Because clinically depressed and Lisa,

00:07:53.687 --> 00:07:56.320
they don't make sense
in that same sentence.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:57.718
And she handed me a prescription

00:07:57.718 --> 00:07:59.213
and I read the prescription,

00:07:59.213 --> 00:08:01.318
it had my name on it and it said Prozac.

00:08:01.318 --> 00:08:02.569
And I thought, "That don't make sense.

00:08:02.569 --> 00:08:04.375
"Lisa Nichols, Prozac,
that don't make sense."

00:08:04.375 --> 00:08:07.993
And I said, "Do you mean I'm sad?"

00:08:07.993 --> 00:08:10.177
She said, "Very, very sad."

00:08:10.177 --> 00:08:11.677
I said, "Can I try something?"

00:08:11.677 --> 00:08:15.988
And I'm not recommending you
guys, if you're on medication,

00:08:15.988 --> 00:08:18.121
you stop taking your meds,
please don't do that.

00:08:18.121 --> 00:08:19.950
I asked my doctor, she agreed.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.741
I said, "Do you mind if I try
something before I take this?"

00:08:22.741 --> 00:08:24.749
She goes, "Yes, but I need
to see you back in 30 days.

00:08:24.749 --> 00:08:25.880
"If you're in the same condition,

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:27.569
"I need us to try this medicine."

00:08:27.569 --> 00:08:29.049
I said, "Okay, I can do that."

00:08:29.049 --> 00:08:30.098
So I went home.

00:08:30.098 --> 00:08:34.265
And every day, I got in the
mirror, and I drilled I am.

00:08:36.498 --> 00:08:37.439
Every day.

00:08:37.439 --> 00:08:41.701
Because I realized I
have forgotten who I was.

00:08:41.701 --> 00:08:42.581
I just forgot.

00:08:42.581 --> 00:08:44.828
And it was okay to forget, I just forgot.

00:08:44.828 --> 00:08:47.995
So every day, every day for 25 minutes

00:08:48.872 --> 00:08:50.809
I just went over the I ams.

00:08:50.809 --> 00:08:55.716
Every day I am, I am, I am,
and then I paralleled that

00:08:55.716 --> 00:08:58.137
with I forgive you for,
than I paralleled that

00:08:58.137 --> 00:08:59.525
with I committ to you, Lisa.

00:08:59.525 --> 00:09:00.875
Every single day.

00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:03.396
I went back in 30 days,
and I'm talking to her,

00:09:03.396 --> 00:09:05.817
and I'm on fire, she's just looking at me.

00:09:05.817 --> 00:09:08.176
And I'm just talking, talking,
she twisted her head again,

00:09:08.176 --> 00:09:10.008
and I'm just talking, talking, she says,

00:09:10.008 --> 00:09:10.841
"Wait, I got to stop you."

00:09:10.841 --> 00:09:11.674
I said, "What?"

00:09:11.674 --> 00:09:14.681
She goes, "What are you
taking? And can I have some?"

00:09:14.681 --> 00:09:17.362
(laughs) I was like,
"I'm taking some of me."

00:09:17.362 --> 00:09:19.091
And so the power of I am,

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:22.670
the power of I am can pull you
through the darkest moment.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:24.162
The power of I am.

00:09:24.162 --> 00:09:28.406
Success is personally defined by everyone.

00:09:28.406 --> 00:09:32.988
And as you're creating success,
create holistic success.

00:09:32.988 --> 00:09:36.066
My biggest successes are the things

00:09:36.066 --> 00:09:37.420
that people don't even see.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:40.067
It's the fact that my 14 year old son

00:09:40.067 --> 00:09:43.058
calls me his best friend to his friends.

00:09:43.058 --> 00:09:46.441
That's bigger than any book
deal that you can give me,

00:09:46.441 --> 00:09:49.232
that's bigger than sitting
across from Larry King

00:09:49.232 --> 00:09:51.653
or beside Oprah, that my 14 year old son

00:09:51.653 --> 00:09:54.498
calls me his best friend.

00:09:54.498 --> 00:09:56.912
Creating holistic success
is really important.

00:09:56.912 --> 00:09:59.438
Let me tell you, in order
to have something different,

00:09:59.438 --> 00:10:01.331
you are going to have to
do something different.

00:10:01.331 --> 00:10:02.762
In order to have something more,

00:10:02.762 --> 00:10:04.571
you have to do something
you haven't done yet.

00:10:04.571 --> 00:10:06.690
I have to say the things
I didn't want to say,

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:08.341
do the things I didn't feel like doing

00:10:08.341 --> 00:10:10.169
to have the life I knew I wanted.

00:10:10.169 --> 00:10:11.002
Period.

00:10:12.656 --> 00:10:13.900
Period.

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:15.698
And all I did was give instructions

00:10:15.698 --> 00:10:17.117
for here, do this bite size,

00:10:17.117 --> 00:10:19.249
do this bite size, do this bite size.

00:10:19.249 --> 00:10:23.027
Bite sized, digestible, palatable
pieces of what you can do.

00:10:23.027 --> 00:10:25.212
Does that sound good to you guys?

00:10:25.212 --> 00:10:26.687
And when you look up, and
you don't have to have

00:10:26.687 --> 00:10:29.078
a magnificent change over 12 months.

00:10:29.078 --> 00:10:30.662
Have a small change over 30 days,

00:10:30.662 --> 00:10:32.112
and then a small change over 30 days.

00:10:32.112 --> 00:10:34.885
You breakthrough will
come in needlepoint moves.

00:10:34.885 --> 00:10:37.030
And you'll look up in five years,

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.043
and not recognize your life.

00:10:39.043 --> 00:10:42.160
- What's been your biggest
accomplishment, you think?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:45.918
- Bouncing back, number
one, is refusing to listen

00:10:45.918 --> 00:10:47.563
to the negative chatter in my own head,

00:10:47.563 --> 00:10:51.444
refusing to listen to other
people's perception of me,

00:10:51.444 --> 00:10:55.311
creating something from
absolutely nothing.

00:10:55.311 --> 00:10:58.978
There's the books, there's the
TV, there's all that stuff,

00:10:58.978 --> 00:11:01.247
but my biggest accomplishment
is being willing

00:11:01.247 --> 00:11:03.912
to give myself a thousand second chances,

00:11:03.912 --> 00:11:08.112
and every time I got
to 999, I press reset.

00:11:08.112 --> 00:11:09.811
I didn't ask permission, I gave notice.

00:11:09.811 --> 00:11:12.187
At some point, I have to stop asking,

00:11:12.187 --> 00:11:13.083
"Can I be great?

00:11:13.083 --> 00:11:13.923
"Can I be brilliant?

00:11:13.923 --> 00:11:16.120
"Can I be okay and still be accepted?"

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.175
I just stopped asking permission

00:11:18.175 --> 00:11:20.459
and just gave notice unapologetically.

00:11:20.459 --> 00:11:21.801
And not in a braggadocios way.

00:11:21.801 --> 00:11:23.721
Not in a way that's shrunk anyone else,

00:11:23.721 --> 00:11:26.378
in a way that's said,
"I only got one life,

00:11:26.378 --> 00:11:28.428
"and Imma ride this one
til the wheels fall off."

00:11:28.428 --> 00:11:30.788
And then all the other stuff came

00:11:30.788 --> 00:11:32.880
as a result of a decision I made.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:33.713
- Right.

00:11:33.713 --> 00:11:34.802
But it was a decision you made.

00:11:34.802 --> 00:11:36.917
- It was a decision, and it didn't come

00:11:36.917 --> 00:11:39.848
from a motivational experience.

00:11:39.848 --> 00:11:41.779
It didn't come from an inspiring teacher,

00:11:41.779 --> 00:11:44.672
it came from hitting rock bottom.

00:11:44.672 --> 00:11:47.645
There's so much value in what you unlearn.

00:11:47.645 --> 00:11:51.028
Sometimes the best thing you
can do is unlearn some things.

00:11:51.028 --> 00:11:54.137
We're always going after
learning something new

00:11:54.137 --> 00:11:55.965
because we're information junkies,

00:11:55.965 --> 00:11:59.226
because we have all these forms
of information coming at us

00:11:59.226 --> 00:12:01.269
on the internet, coming at us in books,

00:12:01.269 --> 00:12:03.690
coming at us on the radio,
coming at us on television,

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.295
that we want to learn, learn learn.

00:12:05.295 --> 00:12:07.019
But sometimes your biggest breakthrough

00:12:07.019 --> 00:12:10.933
is in what you unlearn,
and then you relearn.

00:12:10.933 --> 00:12:14.255
Sometimes you have to disrupt
your soil, pull your soil up,

00:12:14.255 --> 00:12:17.198
take that dry dirt that's
been planted for years.

00:12:17.198 --> 00:12:19.276
I know, I just been
knowing this for years.

00:12:19.276 --> 00:12:20.229
This is what my mother taught me,

00:12:20.229 --> 00:12:21.204
this is what we've always done.

00:12:21.204 --> 00:12:23.355
You have to disrupt that soil

00:12:23.355 --> 00:12:27.148
in order to plant a new
seed to grow a new fruit.

00:12:27.148 --> 00:12:28.200
Yeah, yeah?

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.189
You guys got that?

00:12:29.189 --> 00:12:33.495
And so I came very comfortably
to disrupt your soil.

00:12:33.495 --> 00:12:35.754
That's what I came for,
to disrupt your soil.

00:12:35.754 --> 00:12:38.057
Not to necessarily keep you
comfortable in what you know,

00:12:38.057 --> 00:12:39.019
stay comfortable in that.

00:12:39.019 --> 00:12:41.701
I want to disrupt you in some
things that are new awareness,

00:12:41.701 --> 00:12:43.408
to go "Oh, wait. Hold on."

00:12:43.408 --> 00:12:45.541
Or new awareness about
what you've been doing

00:12:45.541 --> 00:12:47.246
based on what you've known forever

00:12:47.246 --> 00:12:49.412
that doesn't fit your future anymore.

00:12:49.412 --> 00:12:51.850
Because I can guarantee
you every single one of us

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:54.149
who wants something different
then what we're getting,

00:12:54.149 --> 00:12:57.863
we're doing something
unconsciously from old patterns

00:12:57.863 --> 00:13:00.367
that doesn't even serve our future.

00:13:00.367 --> 00:13:02.156
That's when the tongue in your mouth

00:13:02.156 --> 00:13:03.522
and the tongue in your shoe

00:13:03.522 --> 00:13:05.973
are going in two totally
different directions.

00:13:05.973 --> 00:13:08.124
And your job is to line them up

00:13:08.124 --> 00:13:10.294
so that you can move
forward in a powerful way.

00:13:10.294 --> 00:13:14.067
Every single thing you touch
is impacted by your story.

00:13:14.067 --> 00:13:17.310
As an attorney, as a
teacher, as an architect,

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:20.071
there's not one line of
business that you can be in

00:13:20.071 --> 00:13:23.667
that a story and a great story
won't elevate your outcome.

00:13:23.667 --> 00:13:27.938
Every single line of business,
every single line of service

00:13:27.938 --> 00:13:31.068
that you're connected to will be impacted

00:13:31.068 --> 00:13:33.016
and ideally elevated by the level

00:13:33.016 --> 00:13:35.718
in which you're willing to
tell and share your story.

00:13:35.718 --> 00:13:38.295
So let me give you some
guidelines, some parameters,

00:13:38.295 --> 00:13:40.146
what I like to call the bumper rails,

00:13:40.146 --> 00:13:41.539
as if you were going bowling.

00:13:41.539 --> 00:13:42.880
When I go bowling, I ask them

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.177
to put the little bumper rails down

00:13:44.177 --> 00:13:46.341
so my ball can get down the lane.

00:13:46.341 --> 00:13:48.627
So let me set up some bumper rails for you

00:13:48.627 --> 00:13:52.010
so that you understand
what makes a great story.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.589
So one is the willingness to take risk.

00:13:55.589 --> 00:13:58.196
Most people, Vishen, when
they're telling a story,

00:13:58.196 --> 00:14:00.099
they don't want to take a risk,

00:14:00.099 --> 00:14:03.330
so the story has it's
limits on how high it'll go

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:04.505
or how deep it'll go.

00:14:04.505 --> 00:14:07.055
And when you have that, then
you're really not at that part

00:14:07.055 --> 00:14:08.389
that's going to touch my soul.

00:14:08.389 --> 00:14:09.655
So being willing to take a risk.

00:14:09.655 --> 00:14:13.190
Being clear and concise with your stories.

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:17.845
A great story is a show me
story, not a tell me story.

00:14:17.845 --> 00:14:19.009
Now this is the distinction

00:14:19.009 --> 00:14:20.779
that's the game changer for most.

00:14:20.779 --> 00:14:22.682
Most people are telling a story.

00:14:22.682 --> 00:14:25.590
They say, "So let me just share with you

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.081
"a little bit of my story."

00:14:27.081 --> 00:14:29.332
And I'll tell you and then I'll show you.

00:14:29.332 --> 00:14:32.999
So as I was building my life,
there was a time in my life

00:14:32.999 --> 00:14:34.615
that was very difficult, it was very,

00:14:34.615 --> 00:14:37.023
true story, very difficult,
very challenging,

00:14:37.023 --> 00:14:38.334
very uncomfortable.

00:14:38.334 --> 00:14:40.894
I didn't have a lot of money,
I didn't have a lot of hope,

00:14:40.894 --> 00:14:42.674
and things just looked dismal.

00:14:42.674 --> 00:14:44.688
At some point, I had
to turn my life around.

00:14:44.688 --> 00:14:46.407
At some point, I made the decision

00:14:46.407 --> 00:14:48.190
that life had to get better.

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:49.214
I'm telling you that.

00:14:49.214 --> 00:14:50.750
It was decent, you learn about me.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:52.640
Then if I were to show you that story,

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:54.973
I would say six days a week,

00:14:55.933 --> 00:14:58.716
I had to eat beanies and weenies.

00:14:58.716 --> 00:15:02.412
I had to find money in the crevices,

00:15:02.412 --> 00:15:06.859
in the corners of my couch so
that I can get my son milk.

00:15:06.859 --> 00:15:09.783
There were times when
my heart would beat fast

00:15:09.783 --> 00:15:12.785
just at what am I going to have tomorrow?

00:15:12.785 --> 00:15:17.374
At some point, I got sick
and tired of my own story.

00:15:17.374 --> 00:15:19.414
Is this going to be my future?

00:15:19.414 --> 00:15:21.653
No, I can't handle it.

00:15:21.653 --> 00:15:23.496
Notice a difference in that second story.

00:15:23.496 --> 00:15:25.554
- Wow, I completely see that.

00:15:25.554 --> 00:15:26.387
- I just painted a picture.

00:15:26.387 --> 00:15:27.349
Same story.

00:15:27.349 --> 00:15:29.425
Now the second one where you show a story,

00:15:29.425 --> 00:15:31.511
it's going to require more of you.

00:15:31.511 --> 00:15:33.374
It's going to require
you to find the colors.

00:15:33.374 --> 00:15:34.621
What were you thinking?

00:15:34.621 --> 00:15:35.964
What were you experiencing?

00:15:35.964 --> 00:15:37.531
What was going on in your head?

00:15:37.531 --> 00:15:41.217
Instead of telling me you looked
for money, turn and point.

00:15:41.217 --> 00:15:42.769
Now this is anywhere.

00:15:42.769 --> 00:15:44.927
This is anywhere you are doing anything.

00:15:44.927 --> 00:15:46.996
I promise you, you become
a great story teller

00:15:46.996 --> 00:15:49.374
and you will captivate your audience

00:15:49.374 --> 00:15:50.288
no matter what you're doing.

00:15:50.288 --> 00:15:53.671
I have captivated investors,
I have captivated students,

00:15:53.671 --> 00:15:55.208
I've captivated educators

00:15:55.208 --> 00:15:57.755
because I was willing to show the story.

00:15:57.755 --> 00:15:59.810
I call it unpacking the story, Vishen.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.502
Being willing to tell me
what were you thinking,

00:16:01.502 --> 00:16:03.493
what were you feeling,
what were you seeing.

00:16:03.493 --> 00:16:07.379
Think about a story as an oral movie.

00:16:07.379 --> 00:16:08.734
And so in an oral movie, think,

00:16:08.734 --> 00:16:09.913
when you're looking at a movie,

00:16:09.913 --> 00:16:11.156
the first thing they do is they identify

00:16:11.156 --> 00:16:12.409
what state of time is it.

00:16:12.409 --> 00:16:13.242
Is it futuristic?

00:16:13.242 --> 00:16:14.251
Is it in the now?

00:16:14.251 --> 00:16:15.670
Was it back in the day?

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.346
You notice that based on
what people are wearing,

00:16:17.346 --> 00:16:18.788
how they're talking.

00:16:18.788 --> 00:16:20.729
So paint that picture for me.

00:16:20.729 --> 00:16:22.192
Take me to that environment.

00:16:22.192 --> 00:16:23.838
Set the backdrop up for me.

00:16:23.838 --> 00:16:25.648
Show me what you're going through.

00:16:25.648 --> 00:16:27.020
Instead of saying, "I was angry."

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.476
You can tell me you were
angry, but when you say,

00:16:29.476 --> 00:16:32.491
"The hair on the back of
my neck was standing up.

00:16:32.491 --> 00:16:35.461
"I felt the fumes exiting my nose.

00:16:35.461 --> 00:16:37.596
"I thought that my chest was going to pop

00:16:37.596 --> 00:16:40.918
"and I was going to say something
that I'd regret forever."

00:16:40.918 --> 00:16:43.996
Ooh, you just showed me you were angry.

00:16:43.996 --> 00:16:46.412
Take that extra time to unpack it.

00:16:46.412 --> 00:16:48.683
Why will most people not do that?

00:16:48.683 --> 00:16:50.924
Because it requires a
level of vulnerability

00:16:50.924 --> 00:16:52.389
that we're not willing to share.

00:16:52.389 --> 00:16:54.632
Myth number two is that abundance

00:16:54.632 --> 00:16:59.169
is singularly focused on
possessions and money.

00:16:59.169 --> 00:17:00.002
Right?

00:17:00.002 --> 00:17:02.660
It's all about what you
drive, what you live in,

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:03.979
how much money you make.

00:17:03.979 --> 00:17:08.339
When in fact, this couldn't
be further from the truth.

00:17:08.339 --> 00:17:11.385
Wealth is possessions and money.

00:17:11.385 --> 00:17:13.885
Abundance is a 360 experience.

00:17:16.908 --> 00:17:19.408
Abundance is a 360 experience.

00:17:21.185 --> 00:17:24.964
True abundance, true
abundance is your health,

00:17:24.964 --> 00:17:26.702
because if you don't have great health,

00:17:26.702 --> 00:17:28.591
life does not feel good.

00:17:28.591 --> 00:17:32.540
Abundance is relationship,
at the end of your life,

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:35.418
literally, you will measure
the quality of your life

00:17:35.418 --> 00:17:39.062
by the quality of the
relationships you had.

00:17:39.062 --> 00:17:40.159
All the other stuff will fall away.

00:17:40.159 --> 00:17:41.189
That promotion you're thinking about,

00:17:41.189 --> 00:17:42.297
you're wondering about that raise,

00:17:42.297 --> 00:17:44.395
it will fall away in
the area of importance.

00:17:44.395 --> 00:17:45.807
When you get to the end of your life,

00:17:45.807 --> 00:17:47.883
you will begin to look at the
quality of your relationships.

00:17:47.883 --> 00:17:48.784
How your children related to you,

00:17:48.784 --> 00:17:50.460
how your siblings related to you,

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:51.598
do you have love in your life.

00:17:51.598 --> 00:17:53.734
You literally will start
looking at relationships

00:17:53.734 --> 00:17:56.554
at a higher level as you get older.

00:17:56.554 --> 00:18:00.238
So when you mind them now,
you take care of them.

00:18:00.238 --> 00:18:01.611
And I know that for a fact.

00:18:01.611 --> 00:18:05.119
I have a friend who's worth $14 billion.

00:18:05.119 --> 00:18:06.630
Billion, with a B.

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.536
He was just partying at my
house all night long with Lee.

00:18:09.536 --> 00:18:11.491
Four in the morning, go home.

00:18:11.491 --> 00:18:15.312
And he flew in from Canada
to go to my New Year's party

00:18:15.312 --> 00:18:17.736
because he loves my family connection.

00:18:17.736 --> 00:18:19.491
And he doesn't have one.

00:18:19.491 --> 00:18:23.067
He is financially wealthy,
he is relationship broke.

00:18:23.067 --> 00:18:24.349
Does that make sense?

00:18:24.349 --> 00:18:26.756
Abundance is a 360 experience.

00:18:26.756 --> 00:18:29.422
It's about relationships,
it's about health,

00:18:29.422 --> 00:18:31.511
it's about your spiritual groundness.

00:18:31.511 --> 00:18:33.636
That doesn't mean you
have a religious origin,

00:18:33.636 --> 00:18:34.778
it's about can your release.

00:18:34.778 --> 00:18:37.698
Can you forgive, can you
let go, can you be still,

00:18:37.698 --> 00:18:39.997
do you meditate, do you
have time with yourself,

00:18:39.997 --> 00:18:42.909
that has a lot to do with
the quality of your life.

00:18:42.909 --> 00:18:43.992
That ability.

00:18:50.054 --> 00:18:51.592
And I have a message for you.

00:18:51.592 --> 00:18:53.283
A very important message.

00:18:53.283 --> 00:18:56.684
We live in a world where limiting beliefs

00:18:56.684 --> 00:18:58.890
and limited thinking is accepted.

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:01.361
And in some environments,
it's actually encouraged.

00:19:01.361 --> 00:19:04.121
Not to put anyone down
or any institution down,

00:19:04.121 --> 00:19:06.222
but look at our educational system.

00:19:06.222 --> 00:19:09.546
It's bound by who you
can be, who you can't be.

00:19:09.546 --> 00:19:13.580
We're taught that as an
academic excellence student,

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:15.593
you are expected to achieve more.

00:19:15.593 --> 00:19:16.477
Pressures.

00:19:16.477 --> 00:19:19.494
But yet, even inside that
more, that higher achievement,

00:19:19.494 --> 00:19:21.444
there's still a limiting belief there.

00:19:21.444 --> 00:19:23.243
You know, I look at my life today,

00:19:23.243 --> 00:19:25.422
and it's barely recognizable.

00:19:25.422 --> 00:19:28.545
I'm grateful to say I
have six best sellers.

00:19:28.545 --> 00:19:32.020
I sat with Oprah, with Larry
King, on CNN, Good Day LA.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.866
I've traveled all over the world,

00:19:33.866 --> 00:19:36.926
worked in Taipei and
Africa and Kazakhstan,

00:19:36.926 --> 00:19:38.633
but that wasn't where I started.

00:19:38.633 --> 00:19:42.800
I started struggling for 12
years in the educational system.

00:19:43.844 --> 00:19:46.100
Not thinking I was good enough.

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:51.085
The word fail or not pass was
threaded through every year

00:19:51.085 --> 00:19:53.290
in school in some area or another.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.873
And so I graduated, or got out.

00:19:58.229 --> 00:20:01.355
I mean, I graduated, but
what did I graduate to?

00:20:01.355 --> 00:20:05.879
I graduated to more of who I
think I might be able to be,

00:20:05.879 --> 00:20:09.140
or who I couldn't be,
but not my possibility.

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:12.544
I look up and for the first 10, 15 years

00:20:12.544 --> 00:20:15.128
of my adulthood, I struggled.

00:20:15.128 --> 00:20:19.684
I struggled because I didn't
dream big enough at that time.

00:20:19.684 --> 00:20:20.517
I didn't know.

00:20:20.517 --> 00:20:23.064
I felt like my dreams
were covered and smothered

00:20:23.064 --> 00:20:24.896
with the cultural limitations.

00:20:24.896 --> 00:20:27.517
We're defined by who our parents were,

00:20:27.517 --> 00:20:30.551
what our culture can do,
what our community can do.

00:20:30.551 --> 00:20:32.484
So you look at all the areas of our lives,

00:20:32.484 --> 00:20:36.355
financially, mentally, emotionally,
family, geographically,

00:20:36.355 --> 00:20:40.386
and all of those things
kind of put us in a box.

00:20:40.386 --> 00:20:42.071
And some of our boxes are this big,

00:20:42.071 --> 00:20:43.423
so we think they're amazing.

00:20:43.423 --> 00:20:44.692
Some of them are this big,

00:20:44.692 --> 00:20:47.067
and we know they're
choking the life out of us.

00:20:47.067 --> 00:20:50.876
The reality is we're
trained to be realistic.

00:20:50.876 --> 00:20:53.604
To be logical, to stay practical.

00:20:53.604 --> 00:20:55.890
And there's nothing realistic and logical

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:58.314
about Steve Jobs and his journey.

00:20:58.314 --> 00:21:00.296
There's nothing realistic and logical

00:21:00.296 --> 00:21:01.664
about Dr. Martin Luther King

00:21:01.664 --> 00:21:04.027
and his willingness to be radical

00:21:04.027 --> 00:21:06.666
for a change that none of us saw coming.

00:21:06.666 --> 00:21:08.812
There's nothing realistic
about Nelson Mandela

00:21:08.812 --> 00:21:11.189
leaving prison after 27 years

00:21:11.189 --> 00:21:14.846
and leading the largest
forgiveness movement ever.

00:21:14.846 --> 00:21:19.580
There's nothing realistic and
logical about even my journey.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:21.721
Born and raised in
South-Central Los Angelos.

00:21:21.721 --> 00:21:25.505
Having three fights a week
just to get home from school.

00:21:25.505 --> 00:21:27.999
Being told that I was the weakest writer

00:21:27.999 --> 00:21:29.401
my teacher had ever met,

00:21:29.401 --> 00:21:31.639
and that I should never speak in public

00:21:31.639 --> 00:21:34.900
by my speech teacher, to
looking at my life today

00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:38.557
and going on and having a
child before I got married,

00:21:38.557 --> 00:21:42.902
and getting on government's
assistance just to feed my baby.

00:21:42.902 --> 00:21:45.734
Not having money to buy him Pampers,

00:21:45.734 --> 00:21:48.459
and wrapping my son in
a towel for three days

00:21:48.459 --> 00:21:52.140
until I can afford to get
money to buy him Pampers.

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:54.361
I look at my life, and
I wasn't supposed to be

00:21:54.361 --> 00:21:55.611
who I am today.

00:21:56.548 --> 00:21:59.833
Something turned, but it
didn't come from outside,

00:21:59.833 --> 00:22:03.047
it didn't come from my
culture or my community,

00:22:03.047 --> 00:22:04.753
it came from within.

00:22:04.753 --> 00:22:07.435
Who I was committed to
transforming my life into

00:22:07.435 --> 00:22:08.911
just didn't fit.

00:22:08.911 --> 00:22:12.689
It didn't fit realistic,
it didn't fit practical,

00:22:12.689 --> 00:22:14.397
and it didn't fit logical.

00:22:14.397 --> 00:22:17.048
I didn't know how I
was going to get there.

00:22:17.048 --> 00:22:20.734
There were no examples
of how I would get there.

00:22:20.734 --> 00:22:23.588
There was no instructions,
there was no GPS,

00:22:23.588 --> 00:22:25.660
and there wasn't even anyone around me

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:29.185
that had an idea of how to help me.

00:22:29.185 --> 00:22:31.974
All there was was my intuition.

00:22:31.974 --> 00:22:33.839
My internal GPS.

00:22:33.839 --> 00:22:36.814
My internal guide placement
system, and the will,

00:22:36.814 --> 00:22:40.301
and the desire, and the
big dream inside my belly.

00:22:40.301 --> 00:22:42.096
And I was willing to keep at it

00:22:42.096 --> 00:22:44.921
until I burst something
greater than myself.

00:22:44.921 --> 00:22:47.581
In order to live the life you love,

00:22:47.581 --> 00:22:49.675
and love the life you live,

00:22:49.675 --> 00:22:53.284
you have to be willing to step
on the other side of normal,

00:22:53.284 --> 00:22:55.570
on the other side of where people

00:22:55.570 --> 00:22:56.820
give you permission to step.

00:22:56.820 --> 00:22:57.994
You have to be willing to step

00:22:57.994 --> 00:22:59.223
on the other side of realistic.

00:22:59.223 --> 00:23:02.488
You have to be willing to dream big,

00:23:02.488 --> 00:23:06.816
and give yourself a radical
chance for a radical future,

00:23:06.816 --> 00:23:08.997
and the breathtaking possibility.

00:23:08.997 --> 00:23:11.497
It starts with you, I promise.

